WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.957 --> 00:00:17.341
After Fritz had added another seat to his kayak, we were ready to gather oysters.

2
00:00:18.161 --> 00:00:19.802
Jack rode with Fritz in the kayak.

3
00:00:20.562 --> 00:00:23.884
Mother and Franz stayed behind while Ernest joined me on the sailboat.

4
00:00:24.584 --> 00:00:28.185
We arrived in beautiful Pearl Bay, where we worked hard for two days.

5
00:00:29.026 --> 00:00:31.767
The following morning Fritz led us out of the bay.

6
00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:34.788
Jack and Ernest were busy with the sails.

7
00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:40.291
So they did not notice when Fritz waved to me and turned his kayak in the opposite direction.

8
00:00:41.071 --> 00:00:43.252
I watched him quickly vanish behind a point.

9
00:00:43.272 --> 00:00:44.753
"Where's Fritz?"

10
00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:46.194
Jack asked suddenly.

11
00:00:46.214 --> 00:00:49.296
"He wanted to explore more of the coast," I said.

12
00:00:49.316 --> 00:00:53.758
"If he finds something interesting, he may be gone for two or three days."

13
00:00:54.439 --> 00:00:56.840
The boys accepted my explanation without question.

14
00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.942
That evening we sailed into our own Safety Bay.

15
00:01:01.022 --> 00:01:03.964
Five days passed and Fritz still had not returned.

16
00:01:04.744 --> 00:01:08.905
I tried to hide my anxiety but finally decided that we should go looking for him.

17
00:01:09.725 --> 00:01:11.366
Everyone was delighted at the idea.

18
00:01:12.246 --> 00:01:14.647
Even my wife agreed to accompany us in the sailboat.

19
00:01:15.687 --> 00:01:18.768
Our beautiful little boat bounded over the water in the bright sunshine.

20
00:01:19.448 --> 00:01:23.469
We were almost at Pearl Bay when I saw a dark mass just under the water.

21
00:01:23.489 --> 00:01:25.610
"That's a big rock," I said.

22
00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.170
"There's another one!"

23
00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:28.090
shouted Jack.

24
00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.251
"That rock is moving!"

25
00:01:30.531 --> 00:01:31.211
cried Franz.

26
00:01:31.231 --> 00:01:33.852
"That's not a rock," said Ernest.

27
00:01:34.232 --> 00:01:34.973
"That's a whale!"

28
00:01:35.713 --> 00:01:38.496
We watched as the whales rose from the water around us.

29
00:01:38.516 --> 00:01:41.718
"They're coming up to breathe," Ernest explained.

30
00:01:42.579 --> 00:01:43.960
Suddenly Jack grabbed my arm.

31
00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:45.861
"Father, look over there.

32
00:01:46.142 --> 00:01:46.762
Near that rock."

33
00:01:47.583 --> 00:01:51.126
I glanced over just in time to see a native hiding his canoe behind a rock.

34
00:01:51.966 --> 00:01:54.869
The man stood up for a moment and peered intently at us.

35
00:01:55.729 --> 00:01:56.970
Then he ducked behind the rock.

36
00:01:57.731 --> 00:02:00.653
A moment later he came out and started paddling toward us.

37
00:02:01.514 --> 00:02:03.856
"Hoist a white flag to show we're friendly," I ordered.

38
00:02:04.596 --> 00:02:05.776
"And hand me the megaphone."

39
00:02:06.677 --> 00:02:11.378
I seized the megaphone and uttered the few friendly words I knew in the Malay language.

40
00:02:12.218 --> 00:02:15.299
But neither my words nor the white flag produced the right effect.

41
00:02:15.999 --> 00:02:18.720
The native turned his boat and headed back toward shore.

42
00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.561
Jack lost patience and grabbed the megaphone.

43
00:02:22.281 --> 00:02:25.262
"Come here and make friends with us or we'll—" "Stop!

44
00:02:25.642 --> 00:02:26.642
Stop!" I cried.

45
00:02:26.662 --> 00:02:30.543
"You will only alarm the man with your wild words and gestures."

46
00:02:30.563 --> 00:02:32.744
"But look, Father," said Jack.

47
00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:35.101
"He's paddling straight for us again."

48
00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:37.922
"The villain has Fritz's kayak!"

49
00:02:38.382 --> 00:02:39.002
said Franz.

50
00:02:39.863 --> 00:02:42.004
Among the boys only Ernest remained calm.

51
00:02:42.804 --> 00:02:45.725
He took the megaphone from Jack and addressed the man in the kayak.

52
00:02:46.505 --> 00:02:47.546
"Welcome aboard, Fritz!"

53
00:02:47.846 --> 00:02:48.246
he said.

54
00:02:49.007 --> 00:02:52.128
No sooner were the words out of his mouth than we all recognized Fritz.

55
00:02:53.088 --> 00:02:55.589
In a few more minutes he was on board the sailboat.

56
00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.531
Mother threw her arms around him as we peppered him with questions.

57
00:03:00.391 --> 00:03:01.212
"Where have you been?"

58
00:03:01.552 --> 00:03:02.112
asked Jack.

59
00:03:02.708 --> 00:03:04.529
"Why have you been gone so long?"

60
00:03:05.009 --> 00:03:05.670
asked Franz.

61
00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:07.531
"Why were you hiding from us?"

62
00:03:07.791 --> 00:03:08.591
demanded Ernest.

63
00:03:09.812 --> 00:03:10.813
"Slow down."

64
00:03:11.093 --> 00:03:11.773
Fritz laughed.

65
00:03:12.574 --> 00:03:15.175
"I never dreamed you'd come after me in the sailboat.

66
00:03:15.856 --> 00:03:17.436
I thought you must be Malay pirates.

67
00:03:18.237 --> 00:03:21.459
When you addressed me in that language, I was sure you were pirates!

68
00:03:22.219 --> 00:03:23.480
But then I recognized Jack."

69
00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.161
"Do you know a good spot where we can anchor?"

70
00:03:26.301 --> 00:03:26.682
I asked.

71
00:03:26.702 --> 00:03:30.684
"I can lead you to an island where there is a splendid place to anchor."

72
00:03:31.412 --> 00:03:32.953
He gave me a glance full of meaning.

73
00:03:32.973 --> 00:03:37.194
"The island itself contains all sorts of interesting things."

74
00:03:38.055 --> 00:03:41.816
Now that I knew Fritz's expedition had succeeded, it was time to tell my wife.

75
00:03:42.737 --> 00:03:47.299
When she heard about the Englishwoman's message, she was almost overcome with emotion.

76
00:03:47.319 --> 00:03:52.901
"Another human being—another woman!—here with us," she said.

77
00:03:52.921 --> 00:03:55.882
"But why didn't you tell me about her before this?"

78
00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:59.704
"I didn't want to raise your hopes until I was sure," I replied.

79
00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:05.402
It was difficult to conceal our excitement from the boys, who sensed that something was about to happen.

80
00:04:07.283 --> 00:04:10.584
As soon as the anchor was dropped, they eagerly sprang ashore.

81
00:04:11.445 --> 00:04:13.045
We all followed Fritz in silence.

82
00:04:14.126 --> 00:04:17.487
Suddenly the trail ended in front of a shelter made of tree branches.

83
00:04:18.507 --> 00:04:20.288
A cheerful fire burned in front of it.

84
00:04:21.129 --> 00:04:24.130
Fritz dove into the shelter, leaving his brothers behind.

85
00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:29.172
In another moment he emerged, leading a small, handsome youth by the hand.

86
00:04:30.068 --> 00:04:33.750
From his clothing, the young man appeared to be an officer in the English navy.

87
00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:39.412
Radiant with joy, Fritz said, "I would like to introduce Edward Montrose.

88
00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:43.233
Please welcome him into our family circle as a friend and a brother."

89
00:04:43.894 --> 00:04:44.994
I stared at the young man.

90
00:04:45.774 --> 00:04:48.695
For some reason the Englishwoman wanted us to think she was a man.
